## 6. Performance Targets

### Transpilation Speed (for 5,000-line YAML)

| Stage | Target | Justification |
|-------|---------|---------------|
| YAML Parse | ~5 ms | serde-saphyr at 89 MB/s |
| Code Generation | 50-200 ms | Askama pre-compiled (5-10x faster than interpreted) |
| Write Files | 5-20 ms | I/O bound, negligible |
| Compilation (incremental) | 1-5 seconds | ~10K generated lines, modern hardware |
| Compilation (clean) | 2-8 seconds | ~10K generated lines, modern hardware |
| **TOTAL (incremental)** | **1.5-5 seconds** | Sum of stages |
| **TOTAL (clean)** | **2-8 seconds** | Sum of stages |

### Inference Performance

| Configuration | Tokens/Second | Latency |
|--------------|----------------|-----------|
| CPU-only | 1-3 t/s | Baseline for low-power systems |
| LM Studio (Vulkan) | 20-40 t/s | +10ms HTTP overhead |
| Direct llama.cpp (Vulkan) | 40-60 t/s | Zero HTTP overhead |
| Apple MLX | 30-50 t/s | +10ms HTTP overhead |

**Hardware Assumptions**:
- Modern x86_64 system (Ryzen 5900x equivalent)
- 8+ cores, 16GB+ RAM
- SSD storage
- Mid-range GPU (AMD RX 7900 XT or equivalent)

