### 15.5 Agent Spawning Configuration

**Default**: **Require explicit permission** - Agents cannot spawn other agents unless specified

**Rationale**:
- Security: Prevent unauthorized sub-agent creation
- Control: User must explicitly enable spawning capability
- Hierarchical: Top-level agents control spawning

**Schema**:
```yaml
agents:
  - name: controller
    permissions:
      can_spawn: true  # Required to spawn sub-agents
      agent: "all"  # Or specify tool permissions
  - name: worker
    # No can_spawn → cannot spawn sub-agents
```

### 15.6 Loop Timeout Handling

**Strategy**: **Detailed logging with path to attempts, results, and timeout analysis**

**Requirements**:
- Log each loop iteration attempt
- Capture where iteration got stuck
- Summary of what made timeout occur
- Path to last successful state for resumption

**Generated Code Template**:
```rust
struct LoopLog {
    iteration: u32,
    started_at: Instant,
    completed_at: Option<Instant>,
    status: LoopStatus,
    stuck_at: Option<String>,  // Tool or operation name
    stuck_reason: String,         // Why it failed
    result: Option<AgentOutput>,
}

impl LoopTimeoutHandler {
    fn on_timeout(&self, log: &LoopLog) {
        // Log detailed failure summary
        // Provide path to resume from last good state
        // Analyze pattern of timeouts for optimization
    }
}
```

### 15.7 Permission Inheritance

**Default**: **Inheritable** - Step permissions inherit from workflow, workflow from agent

**Rationale**:
- Less verbose YAML (no permission repetition)
- Hierarchical control
- Override only when needed

**Inheritance Rules**:
```yaml
workflow:
  permissions:
    agent: "read-only"  # All steps inherit read-only automatically
  - step: Safe analysis
    # Inherits read-only automatically
  - step: Write report
    permissions:
      agent: "write"  # Override to enable writing
```

### 15.8 Profiling and Metrics

**Level**: **Yes, very detailed metrics**

**Metrics to Collect**:
- **Timing Metrics**:
  - Time to respond (first token)
  - Thinking time (before tool call)
  - Tool execution time (each tool)
  - Loop iteration time
  - Total workflow time

- **LLM Metrics**:
  - Token I/O counts (input tokens, output tokens)
  - Tokens per second
  - Context window usage
  - Memory usage (average)
  - Memory usage at specified intervals (user-configurable)

- **Execution Metrics**:
  - Line-item level logging for each operation
  - Parallel execution support
  - Tool usage frequency
  - Success/failure rates

- **Model Settings**:
  - Model name and version
  - Backend (Vulkan, CUDA, Metal)
  - Context size
  - Temperature, top-k, top-p

- **I/O Logging**:
  - Input prompt IO for different stages
  - Output variable references for stage results

- **Advanced Features**:
  - Parallel execution tracking
  - Smart graceful degradation when local system overwhelmed
  - Orchestration strategies for local context management

**Configuration in YAML**:
```yaml
profiling:
  enabled: true
  level: "detailed"  # | "basic" | "none"
  memory_interval: "10s"  # Optional: log memory at interval
  log_per_line_item: true
  track_parallel: true
```

### 15.9 Default Permissions for New Agents

**Default**: **Custom required** - Must explicitly specify permissions in agent definition

**Rationale**:
- Security by default (no implicit permissions)
- Explicit opt-in (user must think about permissions)
- Clear intent in YAML

**Schema**:
```yaml
agents:
  - name: new-agent
    # No default permissions → error if not specified
    permissions:
      agent: "read-only"  # Required
      tools: ["file-read", "grep"]  # Required
```

