### Updated Decision Framework

| Use Case | Recommended Stack | Rationale |
|----------|------------------|-----------|
| **Standard transpilation** | serde-saphyr, Askama, AutoAgents, tokio, llama-cpp-2, thiserror+anyhow | Proven, fast, production-ready |
| **LLM maintainability priority** | Hypertext/RsHtml, AutoAgents, tokio, llama-cpp-2, thiserror+anyhow | Better for AI code understanding |
| **ML research / custom models** | Candle, tokio, thiserror+anyhow | Pure Rust, GPU acceleration, tensor ops |
| **Visual workflow design** | ADK-Rust, AutoAgents, tokio, llama-cpp-2, thiserror+anyhow | Drag-and-drop builder, active |
| **Maximum API stability** | yaml-rust2, Askama, AutoAgents, tokio, llama-cpp-2, thiserror+anyhow | Migration from deprecated parsers |
| **Embedded/simple agents** | smol, llama-cpp-2, thiserror+anyhow | Simpler ownership, single-threaded |
| **Production observability** | snafu, exn (experimental) | Rich diagnostics, structured errors |
| **Maximum performance** | Monoio (Linux-only), llama-cpp-2 (Vulkan), tokio | High-throughput on Linux |

**Key Insight**: No single "best" stack exists. The optimal choice depends on your priorities: performance, LLM-friendliness, API stability, visual workflows, or embedded constraints.

